{"name":"Silver Fern","hex":"#e1ddbf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver fern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A species of fern, Cyathea dealbata"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver_fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver fern","blocks":[{"text":"Alsophila dealbata, commonly known as the silver fern or silver tree-fern, or as ponga or punga, is a species of medium-sized tree fern, endemic to New Zealand. The fern is usually recognisable by the silver-white colour of the under-surface of mature fronds. It is a symbol commonly associated with the country both overseas and by New Zealanders themselves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Alsophila_tricolor_kz03.jpg/330px-Alsophila_tricolor_kz03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_fern"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver"},{"title":"Silver (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Silver or metallic gray is a color tone resembling gray that is a representation of the color of polished silver."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png/330px-Clemens_Friedell_silver_centerpiece_bowl_top_view_-_HLABG.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg/120px-Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg/250px-Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg/120px-Cyathea_dealbata_%28G.Forst.%29_Sw._%28AM_AK144658%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACyathea_dealbata_(G.Forst.)_Sw._(AM_AK144658).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Sunlit_tree_fern.jpg/120px-Sunlit_tree_fern.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 